{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/258731-gears","id":258731,"title":"Gears?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-16T22:48:50-07:00","id":258731,"title":"Gears?","content":"I often see &quot;gears&quot; related to the GM, but what I don't understand is:<br /> <br /> Well...actual gears? Or metaphorical gears?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/316-jesuncolo","name":"Jesuncolo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar316_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T23:31:02-07:00","id":258768,"title":"","content":"Usually metaphorical, sometimes actual. The poetic &quot;gears&quot; of the God-Machine are used to describe the stranger, telltale signs of infrastructure at work, the odd shapes that form take in order to fulfill occult functions. If there's a gas station in the middle of nowhere that sells brands of chips and soda that don't exist elsewhere in the world, then the sale racks are gears. If there's a beating heart in the school's basement furnace, then the furnace is a gear. If there's a local factory that employs lots of people, who all dress the same, style their hair the same, and move similarly, and nobody seems to know where these people live or who they're related to, those laborers are gears. And, yes, if there's a run-down shack in the middle of the forest, and the cellar is constructed around a big gear embedded in the earth's clockwork, and earthquakes start to occur if you jam the gear, that gear is a gear.<br /> <br /> The gear metaphor is usually used to refer to the phenomena that result from the God-Machine's configurations of concealment infrastructure. It lines up these gears in shapes that result in an occult matrix with the effect of preventing most people, human or supernatural, from being able to register the infrastructure as out of the ordinary. They make you avoid paying attention to the brand name on the bag of chips you buy on your way out. They stop you from wondering who the factory people are, why the factory doesn't employ anyone you actually know, and where these factory people commute from, because they sure as hell don't live here. You don't worry about that stuff. Your eyes slide off the gears.<br /> <br /> This is what people with an Unseen Sense attuned to God-Machine phenomena can perceive. This is what the stigmatics and the demons can see that other people can't. The concealment effects of the God-Machine don't work on them. They're wired differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T01:35:56-07:00","id":258860,"title":"","content":"Does mages ( or other supernaturals ) can perceive the gears as they are? Or is this effect occult their perceptions also?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T02:08:30-07:00","id":258871,"title":"","content":"In the absence of a ruling from Dave B., and going off what he's dropped in Fallen World spoilers and his judgment for preliminary GMC stopgap mechanics before that...<br /> <br /> Mages no longer duplicate the effects of the Unseen Sense. That general ability is now represented by the Mage Sight, whose peripheral, always-on feature only detects the active use of supernatural powers, and explicitly fails to detect powers under supernatural concealment. Active Mage Sight only automatically trumps indirect concealment powers \u2014 that is, stuff that doesn't impose a full &quot;you don't perceive me&quot; effect on you, but just makes you invisible, or silent, or makes your footprints disappear or something \u2014 but appropriate applications of the Mage Sight can provide a roll to contest full concealment powers. The occult condition represented by the Infrastructure influence condition doesn't fall under the category of spiritual conditions mages can directly perceive or manipulate with spellcraft.<br /> <br /> And a sidebar in the Demon corebook, p. 39, seems to indicate that characters don't automatically become able to see the gears by dint of being supernatural.<br /> <br /> So TL;DR, how I'd rule it?<br /> <br /> Vampires, mages, etc. <b>are</b> affected by concealment infrastructure as are normal human beings. Appropriate supernatural powers, however, can <b>contest</b> the God-Machine's local concealment effect to pierce it and see the gears for the duration of the power, if the supernatural being thinks to use them; I'd probably do this as a Clash of Wills against some dice pool improvised based on how strong the local concealment infrastructure matrix is. For mages, these would probably be the Mastigos Mage Sight or, for other mages (or a Mastigos who doesn't want to spend Mana), whatever mental shielding spell they would use similarly to resist a vampire's Obfuscate. For vampires, maybe Uncanny Perception or the Spirit's Touch. And so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T03:06:58-07:00","id":258890,"title":"","content":"For what Arcana would show a mage the Gears is question on what principle the Gears are concealed - is it just simple &quot;you don't see me&quot; Mind thing. Or maybe more elaborate qusai-Prime illusions, using symbols magic. What Arcana would you see for this?<br /> <br /> And very tricky question - how could Prometheans see the Gears?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T03:22:39-07:00","id":258893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/258731-gears?p=258890#post258890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what Arcana would show a mage the Gears is question on what principle the Gears are concealed - is it just simple &quot;you don't see me&quot; Mind thing. Or maybe more elaborate qusai-Prime illusions, using symbols magic. What Arcana would you see for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see arguments for Mind or Prime, same as you. Different projects might even achieve the effect differently.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/258731-gears?p=258890#post258890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And very tricky question - how could Prometheans see the Gears?</div> </div> </div> </div>Barring major overhauls of the Transmutations in 2e, Sensorium would be the obvious purview. Depending on how you interpret the relation of the God-Machine to the Principle in your game, and more practically whether you need Prometheans to be more easily able to pierce concealment or are comfortable making them work harder for it, it could be Aura Sight, could even be detecting occult wavelengths with Firesight, or the Promethean might need to be shown the gears first by a demon or stigmatic and learn enough about the God-Machine to create a custom Transmutation that overcomes mental concealment.<br /> <br /> Crossover games that interpret the God-Machine and the Principle to be very tightly linked might even use Sense Pyros or Sense Flux from the Vulcanus set.<br /> <br /> Getting more creative, a Promethean with an Unchained friend to learn from, whose player has access to Magnum Opus, might develop a Tainted Azoth Transmutation from the study of Spiritus that allows her to convert her Azothic Radiance into the Aetheric Resonance of the Unchained, or simply develop an Unchained variant of the Sense of (Type) Transmutation with the simple effect of seeing through the gears like a demon while the power is in use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}